/-!
# Bernstein sign certificates of the binary quartic lemma at `q_s = 1587/1000`

Paper E, `lem:fqe-binary-quartic` (`renyi_binary_quartic.tex`), BQ-3 and BQ-4 at the fixed order
`q = 1587/1000` (generated by `gen_bq_cells.py`; the identities `p = Σ b_ij B_i B_j` are checked by `ring`).

* `bqK` is `K(q_s, s)`, the degree-14 polynomial with `(15Q)⁴ M(P/Q, s) = (q-1) s⁵ (1-s²)² K(q, s)`;
  all 15 Bernstein coefficients on `[0,1]` are negative, so `bqK_neg : bqK s < 0` on `[0,1]`.
* `bqdM s ξ = ∂M/∂ξ` at `q_s`; on `0 ≤ s < 1`, `s ≤ ξ ≤ 1` it is nonnegative (`bqdM_nonneg`): with
  `ξ = s + τ(1-s)` its tensor Bernstein coefficients of bidegree `(6,3)` are nonnegative on four `s`-boxes.
-/

